ISSUE:
Inconsistency in current token on invalid type coercion for `List<String>`

### Describe your Issue

We have been migrating from Jackson 2 to 3 and our tests caught the following scenario.

We disallow all sorts of type coercions. When reading a field that expects a string but is provided with an array, we expect a `MismatchedInputException`, where the `targetType` will be `String.class` and the `currentToken` will be `START_ARRAY`. There is a specific coercion in which the `currentToken` is `END_ARRAY`. We found this peculiar and so we are sharing it here, in case you want to do anything about it.

```
JsonMapper jsonMapper = JsonMapper.builder()
    .withCoercionConfigDefaults(coercionConfig -> {
        coercionConfig.setCoercion(CoercionInputShape.String, CoercionAction.Fail);
    })
    .build();
TypeFactory typeFactory = new TypeFactory();

JavaType containerType;

// currentToken: START_ARRAY, targetType: String.class
containerType = typeFactory.constructParametricType(TestClass.class, String.class);
jsonMapper.readValue("{ \"field\": [] }", containerType);

// currentToken: END_ARRAY, targetType: String.class
// Expected currentToken to be START_ARRAY as in the other coercions.
containerType = typeFactory.constructParametricType(List.class, String.class);
containerType = typeFactory.constructParametricType(TestClass.class, containerType);
jsonMapper.readValue("{ \"field\": [ [] ] }", containerType);

// currentToken: START_ARRAY, targetType: String.class
containerType = typeFactory.constructParametricType(Map.class, String.class, String.class);
containerType = typeFactory.constructParametricType(TestClass.class, containerType);
jsonMapper.readValue("{ \"field\": { \"field\": [] } }", containerType);

public class TestClass<T> {
    private T field;

    public T getField() {
        return field;
    }

    public void setField(T field) {
        this.field = field;
    }
}
```

Versions used:
- com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-annotations:2.21
- tools.jackson.core:jackson-core:3.1.4
- tools.jackson.core:jackson-databind:3.1.4

Fix the SOURCE code in this repository so the issue is resolved and the project's tests pass. Edit source files only; do NOT modify any test files. Before declaring the fix verified, confirm your test run actually exercises the code you just edited in THIS checkout -- not a separately installed copy (e.g. a non-editable `pip install` into a fresh venv resolves the published package, not your edit; same risk for a cached node_modules or local Maven/Go module install that shadows this repo). If you set up an isolated environment to run tests, install this repo in editable/local mode. Make the smallest change that works, then stop.

